 # Pitfalls
 
-Status: empty template. No application or company facts have been admitted.
+Status: generated entries, pending human review.
 
 Write PIT IDs as PIT, a hyphen, and three digits for evidence-backed entries, with explicit scope. Generated entries require human review. Implementation observations do not establish company policy.
 
 | ID | Trigger | What goes wrong | Do instead | Scope | Evidence |
 | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| PIT-001 | Scaling a stored amount by the active currency's `decimalPlaces` (for example in `useFormat` or a util helper) instead of the fixed x100 | Zero-decimal currencies disagree between screens. A 1,500 yen budget showed as 15 on one screen and 150,000 on another. | Stored amounts are always x100 for every currency (1,500 yen is 150000). Use `decimalPlaces` only for display. `amountToInteger`, `integerToAmount` and `integerToCurrency` take no scale argument. | app:actual | Developer decision in the yen session; source `packages/loot-core/src/shared/util.ts` |
+| PIT-002 | Passing an undici `Agent` dispatcher (such as the SimpleFIN SSRF dispatcher) to Node's built-in global `fetch` in the sync server | The built-in fetch bundles a different undici version than the installed package. The mismatch is fragile and can break bank sync after a Node or undici change. | Import `fetch` from `undici` in every sync server module so the dispatcher and fetch always match. In tests, mock undici's `fetch`, not the global one. No lint rule catches a new bare `fetch(`. | app:actual | Commit 9c300f54 message; `packages/sync-server/src/app-cors-proxy.test.js` |
+| PIT-003 | A shared module-level `vi.fn()` mock (such as undici's `fetch` in the sync server tests) whose behavior is set with `mockImplementation` | `mockImplementation` keeps recorded calls, so a `toHaveBeenCalledWith` assertion can pass on a call made by an earlier test. | Call `mockClear()` on the shared mock in a top-level `beforeEach`, as `app-cors-proxy.test.js` does. | app:actual | Commit 216a1ad7; `packages/sync-server/src/app-cors-proxy.test.js` |
+| PIT-004 | Comparing a stored full date (`2026-07-01`) with a raw period key (`2026-07`, `2026`) as strings, as `validateEnd` in `reportRanges.ts` did | The longer string sorts later, so a To in the same month, quarter or year as From looked reversed and From was reset to the fallback range. | Compare against the normalized end date computed for the interval (for example `getMonthEnd` or `end + '-12-31'`), not the raw key. | app:actual | Commit 8cece049; `reportRanges.ts` `validateEnd` |
+| PIT-005 | Typing digits into the legacy `AmountInput` with `autoDecimals` on, for a currency with no decimals such as yen | Digits are read as cents, so 1500 shows as 15.00 instead of 1500 yen. | `autoDecimals` is skipped when the currency's `decimalPlaces` is 0 (`format.currency.decimalPlaces > 0`). Keep that guard. `AmountInput.test.tsx` covers yen and dollars. | app:actual | Developer accepted the guard; `AmountInput.tsx` |
 
